\ Feed arbitrary-precision signed day counters into the real sauce.
\ The existing 46 visible drops and six-bowl mixer already accept
\ five decimal-wide counters; they do not require native day numbers.
\ This adapter is a limited but real integration point for wide dates.
\ It does not migrate gate coordinates, year traversal or month layout.
\
\ The sauce input's five fields are fully overwritten on each call.
\ Day direction is the only small integer; the other fields are copied
\ as decimal-wide quantities without conversion to machine integers.
\ The calculation reads the chosen input pair, then makes the same
\ deterministic complete sauce used by native-day calculations.
\ CAL compilation and large-coordinate sauce execution are pending.

To copy a wide calendar question into the sauce input:
  Put the wide calendar question's calculation count into the sauce input's calculation count.
  Put the wide calendar question's requested count into the sauce input's requested count.
  Put the wide calendar question's day distance into the sauce input's distance count.
  Put the wide calendar question's day sum into the sauce input's sum count.
  Convert the wide calendar question's day direction to a string.
  Put the string into the sauce input's direction count.

\ Compute the complete, canonical sauce from signed-wide day inputs.
\ No native calendar-day or native day-count variable is involved.
To make the complete sauce for a wide calendar question:
  Answer the wide calendar question.
  Copy the wide calendar question into the sauce input.
  Make the complete sauce.
